eterminate findings (pass1.py:263-281) are re-generated identically unless the cap changes","Two distinct budget concepts exist: the per-plan USD cap (shed_to_budget/cap_override) and the transport per-call `llm_retry_max_attempts` (config.py:509); the plan's 'attempt budget' does not disambiguate which one lifts the shed criteria"],"finding":"The budget-shed re-attempt path may be a deterministic no-op: whether a shed criterion actually re-runs is decided by sizing.shed_to_budget against the per-plan USD budget cap (cap = plan_budget_cap(ctx) or cap_override), which is a pure, deterministic function of the material/policy/criterion set and cap. The plan's 'fresh per-invocation attempt budget' is described in transport-retry terms (analogous to llm_retry_max_attempts) and never states that the per-plan SHED cap is raised or bypassed on retry. If the retry invokes shed_to_budget with the same cap over the same criteria, the same criteria are shed again and the promised re-attempt never issues a model call.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdb1dc9737f6e1d29","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'the retry enumerates the shed set from those recorded findings ... and, under the fresh attempt budget, re-attempts them as missing units'; Acceptance Criteria bullet 2 ('budget-shed units remain missing')","norm_id":"n6130fccbb18d3a08","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Latest INDETERMINATE has a criterion shed to the budget cap; `--retry` under the same effective cap re-runs shed_to_budget, sheds the same criterion again, and returns INDETERMINATE with no model call for it — AC2 unmet"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Specify that on `--retry` the enumerated budget-shed criteria are scheduled OUTSIDE the shed pass (or the per-plan USD cap is removed/raised for the retry invocation) so shed_to_budget cannot re-shed them, and clarify that the 'fresh per-invocation attempt budget' is the per-plan spend 